-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
flowwrench n8n2ap (Python port of the Node.js tool n8n2ap, MIT)

Reads the n8n workflow export format and writes the Activepieces flow template
format. n8n is source-available under the Sustainable Use License; no n8n code
is included. Activepieces is Copyright (c) 2020-2024 Activepieces Inc.; its
consulted non-enterprise contracts are MIT. The bundled output schema
(src/flowwrench/n8n2ap/schema/activepieces-template.schema.json) was written for
this project from those public contracts, so its shape, enum strings and
property names follow that interface; no Activepieces implementation code is
included. The upstream license notice is reproduced in THIRD_PARTY.md.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
flowwrench nodered-merge (Python port of the Node.js tool nrflow-merge, MIT)

Reads the Node-RED flow format (Node-RED: Copyright OpenJS Foundation and other
contributors, Apache License 2.0) and integrates with Git through its documented
merge-driver and textconv interfaces. Neither Node-RED nor Git code is included;
Git is a separately installed program.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
flowwrench openapi2piece (Python port of the Node.js tool openapi2piece, MIT)

Reads OpenAPI 3.0/3.1 descriptions (OpenAPI Initiative, Apache License 2.0) and
generates source code that targets the public Activepieces piece APIs
(Copyright (c) 2020-2024 Activepieces Inc., MIT outside enterprise
directories). The generated piece's own LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY.md come from the
templates in src/flowwrench/openapi2piece/templates/. No Activepieces, OpenAPI
or npm package source is included.

